From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: decoded PCM sink with a bounded tvOS mode

Adds the output's decoded PCM sink: ao_avfoundation_pcm.h and .c decide,
and ao_avfoundation_pcm_av.m drives AVSampleBufferAudioRenderer and
AVSampleBufferRenderSynchronizer. The renderer set-up and buffer handling
follow upstream's ao_avfoundation.m.

On iOS, and on tvOS while ao-avfoundation-max-lookahead is 0, the sink
behaves as upstream's: 100 ms reads driven by readiness callbacks, the
renderer's end time handed to mpv as its audio clock, and a restart on
WasFlushedAutomatically and OutputConfigurationDidChange. The only change
is a "trace edge reset" line at every reset.

On tvOS with max-lookahead above 0 (Vivid sets 4 on AirPlay routes), the
renderer queue is bounded to the larger of max-lookahead and audio-buffer
and filled from a 50 ms timer on the output's queue, with up to four reads
per tick, each behind the prefetch guard, so volume changes are heard
promptly. Every reset installs a new renderer and synchroniser at the next
start, carrying the volume and mute across and moving the restart
observers to the new renderer; notifications from a replaced renderer are
ignored. This mode logs trace edges, a periodic "pcm:" transport line and
the fresh-sink, renderer-failure and restart lines Vivid reads, and asks
for an audio reload when the renderer fails or cannot be replaced.

